<Base title="About" description="Bernardo Paranhos, production engineer, UTFPR Medianeira — why an engineering lens on sleep and biohacking." current="about" canonicalPath="/about/">
  <main class="ls-shell">
    <article style="max-width: 68ch; padding: 64px 0 96px;" class="ls-article">
      <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 600; font-size: 46px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 0 0 28px;">About</h1>
      <p>I'm Bernardo Paranhos, a production engineer trained at UTFPR Medianeira. LongevityStack applies the same discipline I use on a factory floor — bottleneck analysis, process optimisation, failure-mode identification — to sleep, supplementation and cognition.</p>
      <p>I am not a physician. Every page on this site says so, and every claim is traceable to a primary source: study type, sample size, population and funding are declared inline, not buried in a linked PDF.</p>
      <h2>Why an engineer, not a doctor</h2>
      <p>Most sleep and supplement content is written by people optimising for engagement, not for being right. An engineering background doesn't make me more correct than a clinician — it makes me allergic to unsourced claims and comfortable saying "we don't know yet" when the evidence doesn't support a clean answer.</p>
      <h2>How this site makes money</h2>
      <p>Affiliate commissions on hardware and supplements I've actually used, and a newsletter with no sponsored placements. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> for specifics. No banner ads — they would sit against everything this site is trying to be.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
